Guidance for the Completion of Programme Specifications and Template for Programme Specifications 
 The SFC has adopted the following minimum data set for programme specifications as agreed by the Scottish Advisory Committee on Credit and Access (SACCA) (HE/01/05, Annex A): 
 awarding body/institution and status – plus teaching institution, if different; 
 details of accreditation by professional or statutory body; 
 name of final award and location in the Scottish Credit and Qualifications Framework (SCQF) – level and credit points; 
 aims of the programme (this to be a broad general outline that can be maintained as an up to date statement with pointers to further details where appropriate); 
 relevant subject benchmark statements and other external and internal reference points used to inform programme outcomes; 
 programme outcomes; knowledge and understanding; skills and other attributes (this to be a broad outline of the key general and programme specific outcomes with pointers to the location of further details); 
 teaching, learning and assessment strategies (this to be a short statement including any distinctive features and the mode of study, and to include pointers to the location of further details); 
 programme structures and requirements, level, modules, credits and awards (a short statement about any particular/distinctive aspects of the structure but otherwise a pointer to the location of further details); 
 admission requirements and the main opportunities for credit transfer into the programme, for example, an indication of whether or not HNQs are accepted with credit and pointers to further information; 
 pointers to further study-progression routes and any major opportunities for credit transfer out of the programme; and 
 the date at which the programme specification was written or revised. It has also agreed the principle that programme specifications should be aimed at and meaningful to current and intending students. SFC further agreed that the TQI website (now the UNISTATS site) will contain appropriate links to Programme Specifications held on each institutions own website. University of Strathclyde Guidance for t he Completion of Programme Specifications and Template for Programme Specifications Approved: March 2008 

Within Strathclyde, Programme Specifications are also seen as helpful tools for quality assurance and enhancement. Their preparation promotes discussion and reflection on new and existing programmes and ensures that there is a common understanding of the aims and intended learning outcomes for the programmes. They serve as reference points for course approval, monitoring and review. However, the final document must be comprehensible and useful to student users. Producing a Programme Specification is an academic, rather than an administrative activity, and the exact content will be determined by the course team. The attached template is intended to ensure that the minimum data set has been produced for each course and that there is a level of consistency in style across the institution for those accessing these documents through the UNISTATS website. In line with the SACCA model it would be helpful if links were provided to relevant information elsewhere on the website or intranet, so that readers can access an increasing level of detail if required.
